{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation complete in worktree arcticseal-cap-warning (base f20e053aad).\n\nCorrection recorded: AC1 was already satisfied on main by 7cf80009d9 — the cap is the pre-existing config key verify.max_ticket_description_chars (default 8000), read by the plan-review guard (det_floor P4) and the completion precheck. This change adds a THIRD reader rather than a new key, preserving single-sourcing.\n\nDesign: gates.description_cap_warning() computes the notice, reusing _plan_review_gate_applies() — the exact probe the claim path uses — so the warning cannot promise a block the gate would not make. It is computed AFTER the CREATE/EDIT event is appended and degrades to None on any error, so it can never block or alter a write.\n\nChannels per surface: CLI prints 'Warning: …' to stderr (stdout stays pure in text and json modes, exit code 0); the library logs it on the rebar logger (edit_ticket now returns it, create_ticket(return_alias=True) carries description_warning); MCP returns a description_warning result field on CreateResultOut/WriteAckOut, mirroring push_status.\n\nGates: make lint, make typecheck, module-size (800) and the locked complexity ratchet all pass. The ratchet forced two extractions (_warn_stderr, _edit_description_warning) rather than raising locked ceilings, and _lib_writes.py was trimmed to exactly the 800-line cap. 22 new tests in tests/unit/test_description_cap_warning.py; a mutation probe (forcing the helper to return None) kills 9 of them across all three surfaces."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786585557352294001,"uuid":"a0352916-76c2-42bf-8463-217329566c28"}